##🍜 AI Restaurant Recommendation System

An end-to-end restaurant recommendation system that combines traditional recommendation algorithms with an LLM-powered natural-language search interface.

Users can describe what they are looking for in natural language, and the system extracts their preferences, filters restaurants, ranks recommendations, and provides an explanation for each result.

## 🚀 Live Demo

**Web Application:**  
https://forkai.onrender.com

**Backend API:**  
https://forkai-api.onrender.com

---

## 📌 Project Overview

This project was built to explore the complete workflow of building and deploying a recommendation system.

Instead of relying on a single recommendation technique, the system implements several approaches and evaluates them against each other:

- Popularity-based recommendation
- Content-based recommendation
- Collaborative filtering
- Hybrid recommendation

An LLM layer is then added to allow users to interact with the recommendation system using natural language.

For example:

> "I want a cheap Japanese restaurant in Kuala Lumpur with good ratings."

The system converts this request into structured preferences and uses them to find and rank suitable restaurants.

---

## ✨ Features

- 🔎 Natural-language restaurant search
- 🤖 LLM-powered preference extraction using Qwen
- ⭐ Popularity-based recommendations
- 📝 Content-based recommendations using TF-IDF
- 👥 Collaborative filtering
- 🔀 Hybrid recommendation
- 📊 Offline recommendation evaluation
- 💬 AI-generated recommendation explanations
- ⚡ FastAPI backend
- ⚛️ React frontend
- 🌐 Deployed on Render
- 🔐 Environment-based API key management

---

# 🧠 Recommendation System

The project implements four recommendation approaches.

## 1. Popularity-Based Recommendation

The popularity model provides a simple baseline.

Restaurants are ranked based on the number of unique users who interacted with them.

This provides a useful baseline for comparing more personalized recommendation approaches.

---

## 2. Content-Based Recommendation

The content-based recommender uses restaurant information such as:

- Cuisine
- Categories
- Restaurant descriptions

The text information is converted into TF-IDF vectors.

Cosine similarity is then used to measure the similarity between restaurants and the user's query.

The basic flow is:

```text
Restaurant Information
        ↓
      TF-IDF
        ↓
Vector Representation
        ↓
Cosine Similarity
        ↓
Similarity Score
